  "worked_solution": "The best deal is the one with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three bottles. To compute the unit price, we divide the cost by the total number of ounces.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in bottle $A$,  we get\n\n$$\n3.00÷20=0.15\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bottle $A$ is $$0.15$  per ounce.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in bottle $B$,  we get\n\n$$\n4.80÷32=0.15\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bottle $B$ is $$0.15$  per ounce.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in bottle $C$,  we get\n\n$$\n1.80÷10=0.18\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bottle $C$ is $$0.18$  per ounce.\n\nFrom the above, we see that bottles $A$ and $B$ have the lowest unit price. Therefore, bottles $A$ and $B$ are the best deal.",
